eanwhile the assault team land on the  ring station amos survives a sci-fi high  g [ __ ] while bobby makes a more  dignified entrance but the assault goes  badly and many of the team are killed  r.i.p hudson game over man it's game  over in the book the soldiers defending  the ring station are duate's rogue  martians helping marco so bobby loves  the opportunity to get some revenge  against the martian traitors who  betrayed her homeworld bobby goes all  iron man and defeats the enemy but is  forced to destroy the railguns with a  missile which was not the plan they had  hoped to capture the railguns so they  could use them against medina and  against marco when he arrives but bobby  had no other choice in the book it's a  bit different bobby tries to capture the  railguns by just blowing up their power  source but the explosion causes a  reaction from the ring station itself  the entire station turns green and it  physically expands to break the railguns  it's like how it reacted to an explosion  in season three bobby's attack seems to  make the station angry  so this is a reminder that the ring  space is a remnant of a vast and  mysterious alien empire and humanity is  messing with powerful forces that they  do not understand  but either way the railguns are broken  leaving the roci alone and defenseless  with all the power of marco's free navy  burning hard to destroy them  but on the way to the ring marco gets a  message from juarte on laconia duate is  an important ally for marco because  dratic gave him his ships and his  railguns and marco hinted earlier that  he's expecting something more from  juarte soon maybe some secret weapon or  reinforcements or something but now  duate tells marco to get [ __ ] he's on  his own laconia won't help marco anymore  because all along duate was using marco  he only gave marco ships and weapons so  that he'd keep earth and mars busy so  that duate could settle on laconia  undisturbed having marco in the ring  space was a useful buffer so that to get  to laconia people would have to get  through marco first joate's tone is kind  of mean and sarcastic here he enjoys  disrespecting marco but in the book  joate comes off as more respectful and  sincere joate really believes that he's  doing what's best for humanity and  that's part of what makes him so  dangerous duarte says that he has gods  to kill because juarte's mission is to  defeat the mysterious entities in the  ring gates juarte is building a great  laconian empire empowered by alien  technology to save humanity from this  interdimensional threat  so duate and laconia have a really cool  plotline which continues in the next  three expanse books  juarte's rejection is a huge loss to  marco but when philip turns up marco  hides his rage and acts like  everything's going great marco  constantly lies and bullshits everyone  around him he said himself that he tells  people whatever they need to hear the  books emphasize how whenever he fails at  something marco acts like that was  actually his plan all along marco  manipulates everyone including his son  so this season philip questions his  loyalty to marco philip feels guilt for  helping marco kill billions of people on  earth and guilt for killing his friend  johan out of stupid misdirected rage he  meets this guy tedeo and learns that  tadeo had a brother who was killed by  marco's bombs on ceres  last season naomi told philip that marco  made him a murderer and that one day  philip will feel guilt for his crimes  now that day has come  philip is shaken by the death of  rosenfeld and tells marco that it could  have been philip who died but marco  doesn't care and says he'd be proud if  philip died for the cause  last season naomi told philip that marco  would let philip die for him but marco  wouldn't die for philip and now philip  says that she was right  marco gives a big speech about how his  revolution will free the belter people  but philip now sees that's not true  marco abandoned millions of belters on  ceres marco doesn't listen to sandrani's  plans to feed the belt he's more  interested in his personal vendettas  against drama holden and naomi marco's  revolution only really serves himself  and philip finally sees that his father  is nothing more than a selfish  manipulative murderer  last season naomi told philip that  sometimes the only choice is to walk  away and so now philip walks away he  leaves marco on his own ship and finally  escapes his controlling father he  rejects the inaros name and instead  names himself philip nagata after his  mother  naomi never finds out that philip  escaped marco but her words free her son  the rosie crew stand alone in the ring  space apparently sarah connor and duncan  idaho didn't make it they're outnumbered  and outgunned by marco's free navy so  they prepare for a heroic last stand but  then naomi comes up with a plan to wake  the mysterious alien entities these  entities have been destroying ships that  go through the ring like the barqueth  last season naomi and the scientist elvi  figured out that these entities become  active after a certain amount of mass  and energy goes through the ring so just  as marco arrives the rosie crew throw  the gm batista through a ring to  activate the entities and so marco is  obliterated along with his navy  it's kind of like gollum dying amidst  orange cgi at his moment of victory in  lord of the rings there's even a ring  in the books when the entities kill  people people experience changes to  their perception and consciousness in  marco's last moments he stops seeing  objects and instead sees the molecules  those objects are made of and the  photons bouncing off them instead of  hearing sound he perceives the  vibrations in the air his sense of self  melts into a cloud of energy before the  entities slither through the nothingness  and sweep him to oblivion the entities  manipulate consciousness itself as a  weapon and these ideas are explored more  in the last few expanse books  so the rosi crew kill marco and finally  end this war the horror for naomi is  that she believes she has killed her son  philip never knowing that philip  actually left marco and survived  inspired by her words  later naomi says that all we can do is  try to help others it doesn't matter if  we ever know that we made a difference  it's not about making ourselves feel  good but the right kind word might  change someone's life so it's always  worth trying  there's a big meeting with the leaders  of earth mars and the belt to figure out  the architecture by which we try to  unfuck ourselves as avasarala says in  the books  she says war doesn't end on the  battlefield war ends at the negotiating  table because killing marco was the easy  part the hard part is making a peace  that will last  unless they can build a more fair and  stable political order they'll just end  up with more war in the future as  drummer said extremists like marco are  inevitable in a system that is unjust  and unequal for belters  the big problem especially in the book  is that the belt doesn't have a future  the whole reason why belters exist was  originally to mine resources in the  asteroid belt over the generations their  culture and bodies adapted to life in  low gravity but now through the ring  gates there are thousands of new  habitable planets with free air and  water where it's way easier to get  resources these new worlds are the  future of humanity but belters have no  place in this future because most  belters like naomi can't survive on  planets with gravity because their  bodies are adapted to space and those  belters who can live on planets within a  few generations won't be belters anymore  the belters as a people and a culture  face extinction  marco's solution to this problem was to  block off the ring gates so that earth  and mars would still need the belt he  wanted to preserve the status quo just  with belters in charge instead of the  inner planets but now the leaders of  earth mars and the belt find a better  solution looking to the future instead  of to the past they form a transport  union to govern the shipping and trade  between the ringgates it's really  important to have someone coordinating  ring transits because otherwise people  might accidentally get eaten by the  entities and there needs to be a lot of  trade right now because since marco  broke earth and was blocking off the  ring gates the colony worlds and damaged  earth are desperate for each other's  resources plus many people want to leave  earth and mars to settle the new worlds  so there's a lot of work to be done  coordinating transport and trade in  space and belters are the best people to  do it the belter's new hope for an  economic and political future is to  become galactic shipping magnates  in the book holden jokes that they  should call the union the spacing guild  which is a reference to a similar thing  in dune  so everyone agrees that a transport  union is a good idea but they can't  agree on who should be in charge of it  after a century of conflict the inner  planets and the belters don't trust each  other avasarala suggests that holden  should be in charge because he has  worked with earth's martians and belters  fairly he has experience with ring space  from medina station and you know he's  the protagonist and he's very handsome  so of course he should be in charge  holden agrees to be the first president  of the transport union the brave warrior  protagonist becomes king in the end like  aragorn in lord of the rings or the  bloody povenzi kids but in an unexpected  twist holden immediately steps down and  makes drummer the new president instead  he says that if the transport union is  the future for belters it should be led  by a belter and drummer is more  qualified for this than holden she has  experience running medina station in the  ring space she was medina's captain back  when it was the behemoth drummer did  shipping and distribution work bringing  supplies to series which is the sort of  thing the transport union will do  drummer has proven her commitment to the  belt over and over and she's shown a  willingness to cooperate with earth and  mars  drama was always the quintessential  belter and after six seasons of struggle  she brings hope for her people  it's also a great character moment for  holden to pull off this sneaky trick he  pretended to agree to be president under  certain conditions plotting all along to  give it to drummer cause holden's whole  thing in the beginning of the series was  to be honest and open about everything  he thought he knew what was best for  everyone he made the decisions and he  told everyone his true intentions but  this time he hides his true intentions  and gives the power to choose to someone  else it shows how much holden has  changed and grown from the naive  idealist he once was  people like miller and avasarala taught  holden that sometimes you've got to lie  for the greater good naomi and drummer  showed holden that he needs to share  leadership with others he is not  personally responsible for running the  universe saving humanity is a group  project  clarissa gives amos a badge of a devil  face amos used to wear one like this but  apparently he lost it last season  clarissa now replaces it and makes one  for herself as a super adorable symbol  of their friendship though the badge has  a dark backstory  in the expanse origins comic book we see  amos and his friend saru when they were  sexually exploited as children saru  committed suicide but he gave amos his  devil badge telling amos to live and to  keep smiling  so the devil badge represents amos  hiding his trauma behind a mask being  emotionally detached to survive  but over six seasons amos grows and uses  his experience of trauma to help others  transforming a symbol of pain into one  of connection and hope  at the end of the expanse holden says we  still don't know what's going on with  the proto-molecule and laconia and  juarte at the end of the credits we see  the entities still lurking in the ring  the expanse tv show is ending without  finishing the story from the last three  expanse books  but the creators of the expanse say that  they're just pausing the story and that  the last three books might be adapted  someday  holden is eager to face this future but  naomi says let's just stay and enjoy the  moment in the present as the rosie sails  the vast expanse  the expanse is about spaceships and  aliens and explosions and it's really  about the tragedy of human conflict no  matter how far we expand into the  universe our politics and our tribes  divide us  heroes are those who try to unite us at  the end of the expanse everything has  changed humanity has expanded from just  one solar system to new worlds across a  thousand stars  earth is devastated mars is obsolete the  belt is transformed but all the old  divisions remain this isn't the end of  war  so everything's changed and nothing's  changed really  at the end of book six anna and her  family head for a new life on a new  world she thinks no matter how far  humanity expands we're basically stuck  with each other we're spending our lives  together in this universe and all we can  do is try to get along  if we're gentle maybe the stars will be  better off with us  thanks for watching and thanks to amazon  prime video uk for sponsoring this video  you can check out the bonus scenes for  season 6 on amazon prime video by  clicking on xray then bonus features  please like and comment and subscribe to  this channel and to alt shift x  cheers  you
 

